IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `K2-art-2b`

-- ============================================================================
-- K2-art-3.l4 -- ARTICLE 3 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: TERRITORIAL SCOPE (layer 1), AND THE COMBINED
-- ANSWER "THIS REGULATION APPLIES".
-- Written by K2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 29-35 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt.
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN.
--
-- THE THREE LIMBS.  Art 3(1), (2) and (3) each say "This Regulation applies to the processing of personal
-- data ..." in one situation.  A limb function answers whether ITS situation is met, and is named for the
-- limb, not for the Regulation, because a limb alone does not say that the Regulation applies (it takes the
-- material scope of Art 2 and the exclusion of Art 2(3) as well).
--
-- THE COMBINED ANSWER.  `Art 3 this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data` is the one place
-- where the three answers meet: it takes P1's material-scope answer as the input PLAN-P1.md section 4.1 names,
-- `Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, a plain
-- input here because a later part cannot import a P1- module), the Art 2(3) fact, and the facts of the three
-- limbs.  Reading of the combination (fork FK3-2): Art 2 and Art 3 are both required, in that an Art 2(2)
-- exception ("does not apply") or an Art 2(3) displacement stops the Regulation whatever Art 3 says.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 3(1): the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment in the Union`

-- src:29 | Article 3
-- src:30 | Territorial scope
-- src:31 | 1. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union, regardless of whether the processing takes place in the Union or not.
@ref Art 3(1) establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union (src:29-31)
GIVEN `the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing takes place in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3(1) the territorial limb: the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union` MEANS
    IF `the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 3(1) names one situation, "in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union", and does not say "only"; Art 3(2) and (3) name others, and for a processing in none the text does not say
    -- "regardless of whether the processing takes place in the Union or not": `the processing takes place in the Union` is not read, by the text's own words.

§ `Article 3(2): a controller or processor not established in the Union, data subjects in the Union`

-- src:32 | 2. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data of data subjects who are in the Union by a controller or processor not established in the Union, where the processing activities are related to:
-- src:33 | (a) the offering of goods or services, irrespective of whether a payment of the data subject is required, to such data subjects in the Union; or
-- src:34 | (b) the monitoring of their behaviour as far as their behaviour takes place within the Union.
@ref Art 3(2)(a) and (b) offering of goods or services; monitoring of behaviour (src:32-34)
GIVEN `the data subjects are in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller or processor is not established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing activities are related to the offering of goods or services to those data subjects in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a payment of the data subject is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing activities are related to the monitoring of the behaviour of those data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `their behaviour takes place within the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3(2) the territorial limb: the processing is of data subjects in the Union by a controller or processor not established in the Union, and the activities are related to offering goods or services or to monitoring behaviour` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the data subjects are in the Union`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 3(2) is about "data subjects who are in the Union"; a data subject elsewhere is outside it and the text does not say
        IF NOT (`the controller or processor is not established in the Union`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 3(2) is about "a controller or processor not established in the Union"; one that is established there is Art 3(1)'s case
        IF `the processing activities are related to the offering of goods or services to those data subjects in the Union` OR (`the processing activities are related to the monitoring of the behaviour of those data subjects` AND `their behaviour takes place within the Union`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b), a marginal reading, FK3-1): "where the processing activities are related to: (a) the offering of goods or services, irrespective of whether a payment of the data subject is required, to such data subjects in the Union; or (b) the monitoring of their behaviour as far as their behaviour takes place within the Union"
        -- "irrespective of whether a payment of the data subject is required": `a payment of the data subject is required` is not read, by the text's own words.
        -- "as far as their behaviour takes place within the Union": read as a requirement that the monitored behaviour takes place in the Union (fork FK3-4); no single input could carry a partial answer.

§ `Article 3(3): a controller not established in the Union, in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law`

-- src:35 | 3. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data by a controller not established in the Union, but in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law.
@ref Art 3(3) Member State law applies by virtue of public international law (src:35)
GIVEN `the controller is not established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3(3) the territorial limb: the processing is by a controller not established in the Union, in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law` MEANS
    IF `the controller is not established in the Union` AND `the processing is in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 3(3) names "a controller not established in the Union" and "a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law"; "where" here describes the place, not a gate on a duty, so a case outside it is not a failed gate (fork FK3-3)

§ `Article 3: this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data (the combined answer)`

-- src:29 | Article 3
-- src:30 | Territorial scope
-- src:31 | 1. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union, regardless of whether the processing takes place in the Union or not.
-- src:32 | 2. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data of data subjects who are in the Union by a controller or processor not established in the Union, where the processing activities are related to:
-- src:33 | (a) the offering of goods or services, irrespective of whether a payment of the data subject is required, to such data subjects in the Union; or
-- src:34 | (b) the monitoring of their behaviour as far as their behaviour takes place within the Union.
-- src:35 | 3. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data by a controller not established in the Union, but in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law.
@ref Art 3 territorial scope, with Art 2(1) and (2) and Art 2(3) (src:29-35)
GIVEN `Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the processing is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing takes place in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subjects are in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller or processor is not established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing activities are related to the offering of goods or services to those data subjects in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a payment of the data subject is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing activities are related to the monitoring of the behaviour of those data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `their behaviour takes place within the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is not established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3 this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`Art 2(3) this Regulation applies to the processing, where it is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` `the processing is by the Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (marginal reading FK2-1, the text says no only by naming another instrument): "For the processing of personal data by the Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, Regulation (EC) No 45/2001 applies."
        IF `Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- (fork FK3-2: the answer of Art 2 and the answer of Art 3 are both required)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): in Article 2, "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data" in the cases of Art 2(2)
        IF `Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the material scope is P1's answer, and it does not answer on these facts
        IF ((`Art 3(1) the territorial limb: the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union` `the processing is in the context of the activities of an establishment of a controller or a processor in the Union` `the processing takes place in the Union`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           OR ((`Art 3(2) the territorial limb: the processing is of data subjects in the Union by a controller or processor not established in the Union, and the activities are related to offering goods or services or to monitoring behaviour` `the data subjects are in the Union` `the controller or processor is not established in the Union` `the processing activities are related to the offering of goods or services to those data subjects in the Union` `a payment of the data subject is required` `the processing activities are related to the monitoring of the behaviour of those data subjects` `their behaviour takes place within the Union`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           OR ((`Art 3(3) the territorial limb: the processing is by a controller not established in the Union, in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law` `the controller is not established in the Union` `the processing is in a place where Member State law applies by virtue of public international law`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): each limb of Art 3 says "applies" in one situation and none says "only", so a processing that meets none of the three is not decided by the text (fork FK3-1; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
